Understood: you want a `clear()` method on `Cart` that removes every line.

Added it to `src/cart.ts`:

```ts
clear(): void {
  this.lines.clear();
}
```

Placed after `remove()` and before `items()`, matching the class's existing style (a `Map` backing store, so `lines.clear()` empties it and leaves `items()` returning `[]` and `subtotal()` returning `0`).

Verified with `npm run test` — 5 tests, 5 pass, 0 fail. Note the existing suite has no test for `clear()`; I did not add one since you did not ask for it, but I can if you want coverage.
